{
  "chalk": 1,
  "name": "07-effectively-once.chalk",
  "cells": [
    {
      "src": "Effectively-once delivery",
      "type": "section",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "> [!goal]\n> Model a channel that may deliver a message twice, and see that an idempotent handler gives each message its effect exactly once while a non-idempotent one does not.",
      "type": "markdown",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "A network that guarantees delivery retries, and retries duplicate. **Exactly-once delivery** is not something a network can promise; **effectively once** is: deliver at least once, and make applying a message twice the same as applying it once.",
      "type": "markdown",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "let Dup = system(\n  var sent in 0..1\n  var copies in 0..2\n  var applied in 0..3\n  init sent = 0 ∧ copies = 0 ∧ applied = 0\n  action send when sent = 0 do sent := 1, copies := 1\n  action duplicate when copies = 1 ∧ applied = 0 do copies := 2\n  action deliver when copies > 0 do copies := copies - 1, applied := applied + 1\n)",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "invariant(Dup, applied ≤ sent)",
      "showWork": true,
      "label": null,
      "stepwise": 0
    },
    {
      "src": "The handler adds each delivery to a count, so a duplicate doubles the effect. An idempotent handler records that the message was seen:",
      "type": "markdown",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "let Idem = system(\n  var sent in 0..1\n  var copies in 0..2\n  var seen in bool\n  init sent = 0 ∧ copies = 0 ∧ seen = false\n  action send when sent = 0 do sent := 1, copies := 1\n  action duplicate when copies = 1 do copies := 2\n  action deliver when copies > 0 do copies := copies - 1, seen := true\n)",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "invariant(Idem, seen = true → sent = 1)",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "eventually(Idem, seen = true)",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "Here every run delivers, because delivering is all the system can do once the message is sent. In a real system other work competes for the same machine, and it is fairness that guarantees delivery: a liveness question for the channel, separate from the handler's safety.",
      "type": "markdown",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "In Lean",
      "type": "section",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "/-- A handler that adds to a balance: a duplicate is applied twice. -/\ndef credit (balance : Nat) (amount : Nat) : Nat := balance + amount\n\nexample : credit (credit 0 5) 5 ≠ credit 0 5 := by decide\n\n/-- A handler that records a message id in a set. -/\ndef record (seen : List Nat) (m : Nat) : List Nat := if m ∈ seen then seen else m :: seen",
      "type": "lean",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "theorem record_idempotent (seen : List Nat) (m : Nat) : record (record seen m) m = record seen m := by",
      "type": "exercise",
      "lean": true,
      "prompt": "Prove that recording a message twice is recording it once.",
      "leanSolution": "  unfold record\n  by_cases h : m ∈ seen <;> simp [h]",
      "hints": [
        "Unfold `record` and split on whether `m` was already seen."
      ],
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "Exercises",
      "type": "section",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "invariant(Dup, applied ≤ sent)",
      "type": "exercise",
      "prompt": "Does the counting handler apply each message at most once?",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "invariant(Idem, seen = true → sent = 1)",
      "type": "exercise",
      "prompt": "Is the idempotent handler's effect always backed by a sent message?",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    },
    {
      "src": "> [!summary]\n> Retrying networks duplicate. Effectively-once processing is at-least-once delivery plus an idempotent handler, and idempotence is a one-line theorem about the handler, not a property of the network.",
      "type": "markdown",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    }
  ],
  "scenes": []
}
